## 6. Daoist vocabulary, historically disciplined

This section states the historical material the Leader asked be tested, using only the five supplied external sources, and observing the caution the commissioning office explicitly required.

**Taiji (Â§™Ê•µ, "Supreme Ultimate/Ridgepole").** Per SEP "Chinese Metaphysics," taiji is rooted in *Yijing* cosmology and given its most influential systematic development by the **Song** Neo-Confucian philosopher **Zhou Dunyi (1017‚Äì1073)** in the *Taijitu shuo* ("Explanation of the Diagram of the Supreme Ultimate"), where the formula "ÁÑ°Ê•µËÄåÂ§™Ê•µ" ("wuji er taiji") pairs the two terms and describes taiji as generating the phenomenal world through alternating movement and stillness (yang/yin). **[HISTORICAL CLAIM, sourced to SEP "Chinese Metaphysics."]**

**Wuji (ÁÑ°Ê•µ, "Non-Ultimate"/"Limitless").** Paired with taiji in the same Song formulation; also present in the broader Daoist cosmological vocabulary summarized by SEP "Religious Daoism," which describes the Dao itself in terms of wuji and taiji together with precosmic stages of shen (spirit), qi (vital energy), and jing (essence). **[HISTORICAL CLAIM, sourced to SEP "Religious Daoism."]**

**The required caution, stated explicitly:** Zhou Dunyi's *Taijitu shuo* is a **Song-dynasty (960‚Äì1279) Neo-Confucian** text. It must not be labeled Ming Daoism. This report does not so label it anywhere.

**Xiantian qi (ÂÖàÂ§©Ê∞£, "precosmic"/"prior-to-form" vital energy).** SEP "Religious Daoism" summarizes internal-alchemy (neidan) cosmology as organized around precosmic stages of shen/qi/jing, distinguished from their postnatal (houtian) counterparts ‚Äî xiantian qi is the primordial vitality cultivated in practice, as opposed to acquired postnatal qi. **[HISTORICAL CLAIM, secondary-source only.]**

**The Ming carrier.** The *Xingming guizhi* (ÊÄßÂëΩÂú≠Êó®, "Principles of Nature and Life") is a genuinely **Ming-dynasty (1368‚Äì1644)** text, dated 1615, per the Chinese Text Project bibliographic entry and the Chinese Religious Text Authority entry C71: a syncretic, illustrated neidan work. **[HISTORICAL CLAIM, bibliographic sourcing only ‚Äî I have not seen the primary text.]** The supplied Brill specialist chapter ("Visualizing Perfection") treats the *Xingming guizhi*'s alchemical-body imagery and describes visualization as a transformative practice oriented toward fundamental cosmic order. **[HISTORICAL CLAIM, specialist-source, one-line summary only.]**

**Primary-source and specialist-source gaps, stated explicitly, as required:**
- I have no access to the *Xingming guizhi*'s own text. I cannot state how, or whether, it itself uses "taiji," "wuji," or "xiantian qi" as technical terms, in what configuration, or with what argument. The CText/CRTA entries are bibliographic identifications, not content.
- I have only a one-line gloss of the Brill chapter's argument. I do not know its treatment of specific diagrams, its dating apparatus, its engagement with the Song wuji-taiji lineage, or its position on continuity/discontinuity between Song Neo-Confucian and Ming neidan uses of the terms. Any elaboration beyond the supplied summary would be invented and is withheld.
- Whether Zhou Dunyi's taiji diagram itself has Daoist diagram antecedents is a matter of ongoing sinological discussion; the supplied sources do not adjudicate it, and this report does not assert a lineage either way.

---

## 7. Testing the taiji comparison against the distal bypass, precisely

With ¬ß2 fixed and ¬ß6 stated, the comparison can now be tested rather than asserted.

**The candidate structural rhyme.** Taiji names a generative bipolar differentiation (yin/yang) arising from ‚Äî or paired with ‚Äî an undifferentiated wuji. The distal bypass's step 2 is a bipolar classification (damage/border) arising from a prior undifferentiated territory of overlapping local records. Both, read loosely, are "one field splits into two kinds under some generative/analytic operation."

**Where the rhyme breaks, precisely:**

1. **Cardinality mismatch.** The distal bypass's proved protected-difference carrier is **FOUR**-valued (neither/for/against/both ‚Äî Source 5, `four_initial`, zero-axiom **[THEOREM]**), not two-valued. Classical yin/yang cosmology, and the Yijing's combinatorics built from binary lines, is fundamentally dyadic in its generative step. A four-valued paraconsistent lattice and a binary generative cosmology are not the same shape, and no map between them has been constructed here or shown to exist.
2. **Process vs. procedure.** Taiji, as summarized by the supplied SEP entries, is a continuous cosmogonic process (movement and stillness alternating without terminus). The distal bypass's classification is a terminating, decidable procedure applied once per obstruction, followed by discharge or certification. One is dynamics; the other is a decision.
3. **No named formal carrier.** Source 3 ¬ß11 of the corpus itself states the applicable discipline exactly: *"A concept is earned when the structure it names is the unique object, up to isomorphism, forced by an explicit list of requirements ‚Äî and is otherwise an unpriced identification of a word with a thing. ... An analogy identifies the roles of two structures, so it is either proved ‚Äî an isomorphism, thereafter a theorem and no longer an analogy ‚Äî or refused, as decoration that costs exactly the confusion it later purchases."* No such requirement list has been stated for "taiji ‚âÖ distal bypass," and none is proposed here. Under the corpus's own rule, this analogy is **refused as decoration** until such a list exists ‚Äî not asserted, not adopted, held at metaphor.

**Verdict:** the taiji comparison is **[METAPHOR]** only. It may be pedagogically evocative ‚Äî a way of gesturing at "unity differentiates into a working duality" ‚Äî but it transfers no formal content, and the corpus's own naming discipline (which this report is applying to itself, for consistency) forbids treating it as more than that without a proof that does not currently exist and was not requested to be constructed.

**Wuji as a gloss on pre-settlement territory.** Source 11 ¬ß2 already has its own unproved metaphor for this ‚Äî "liquid, underdetermined information" settling into "glassy" formation ‚Äî and flags it explicitly: *"The language of informational Lorentzian lightcones remains a research interpretation until its relation to these evidence conditions is formally stated and proved."* Overlaying wuji on top of an already-flagged, already-unproved physics metaphor does not add rigor; it stacks two unproved figurative layers. This report declines the stack and keeps them separate: liquid/glassy is one **[OPERATIONAL INTERPRETATION]**, wuji is a different **[METAPHOR]** from a different tradition, and neither licenses the other.

**Xiantian qi as a gloss on the exogenous pulse.** Same verdict, for the reason the commissioning brief itself anticipates: qi, in the supplied sources, names a cultivated vitality within a specific embodied, ritual, and ‚Äî per the Brill chapter's one-line gloss ‚Äî visualization-based religious practice tradition. It is not, in any supplied source, a measurable quantity with an established unit. Reading $p_M(t)$ as "xiantian qi" would be exactly the category error the commissioning brief warns against, and the corpus's own instrument discipline independently forbids it (¬ß8 below).

**An additional caution the corpus itself supplies, and which applies squarely here.** Source 10 (the ethnomathematics survey) spends its entire methodology and ethics sections on precisely this failure mode: formalizing a living cultural or religious practice for an unrelated instrumental purpose, without the practice's own authority, is extraction, even when done with mathematical care. Neidan is a living religious-practice tradition with its own textual, ritual, and community authority; it is not a dead formalism available for free reuse as engineering vocabulary. This report treats the same caution as applying to Daoist internal-alchemy vocabulary here, by direct analogy to Source 10's own stated discipline ‚Äî this is itself flagged as **[NEW CONSTRUCTION, THIS REPORT]**, an extension of Source 10's ethics to a new domain, not a claim already made anywhere in the corpus.

---

## 8. The correspondence matrix

| Leader term | Corpus carrier | Historical Daoist source/scholarship | Proposed correspondence | Epistemic status | Incompatibility / falsifier |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| "ANT-Colony Pulsar" | ACO (Source 9), stigmergy lineage (Source 8), settlement/climate (Source 1) | None (astrophysical name only) | Exogenous, possibly periodic signal external to a settlement's admitted evidence, loosely analogous to a persistent trace field | **[NEW CONSTRUCTION]** / **[METAPHOR]**, untested | No observed periodic MetroPlat signal exists (¬ß1); ACO's H1‚ÄìH4 have no defined analogue for this channel (¬ß5) |
| MetroPlat's "external cadence" | MetroPlat as external settlement (Sources 2, 11) | None | Sense 1 of six (¬ß4) | **[EVIDENTIARY GAP]** | Premise itself unlogged; requires instrumentation before any typed claim is possible |
| Distal bypass as "taiji of the ANT colony" | Obstruction sheet, damage/border classification, certificates, least-fixed-point settlement (Source 2) | SEP "Chinese Metaphysics" ‚Äî taiji in Yijing/Song Neo-Confucian cosmology, esp. Zhou Dunyi | Generative bipolar differentiation (yin/yang) as a gloss on damage/border classification | **[METAPHOR]**; refused as decoration under Source 3 ¬ß11's own rule pending a proof that does not exist | Protected-difference carrier is proved **FOUR**-valued, not binary (Source 5, `four_initial`); taiji is continuous process, distal bypass is a terminating decision procedure; no isomorphism requirement list stated |
