# The strange math: a training note for future agents

2026-07-11. Operator-requested. This note carries the *perspective* layer the
Lean and blueprint cannot: what the results of this period mean, how they
connect to each other and to outside mathematics, and what a future agent
should know before touching the frontier. Every claim below is marked
theorem (proved in Lean, cite by declaration name) or conjecture/reading
(not proved; do not cite as fact).

## 0. What this system is

Infomaterial is best understood not by its own generative rhetoric but as a
**formal metrology of inconsistency**: a measurement theory for
contradiction, in which cohomology is the accounting system. The load-bearing
results are all of one shape ‚Äî *what does it cost, in held ‚ä§, to merge local
views that disagree?* The exchange theorems in quantum contextuality, the
coordination-cost cycle ranks, the Landauer ledger, the six-term long exact
sequence whose connecting map is nonzero exactly when a settling step is
irreversible, the percolation excess-contact pricing: one subject. No other
body of mathematics has this as a proved exchange web; the pieces exist
separately in Abramsky's contextuality, Hellerstein's CALM theorem,
Landauer's principle, and Toulouse's frustration theory.

