## 1. Contradiction is a compactification artifact

The single strangest proved fact. Two theorem families, read together:

- **FOUR is initial among bounded interlaced bilattices**
  (`Infomaterial.four_initial`, `four_rigid`, and the bound-exchange
  identities `InterlacedBilattice.joinK_tTop_tBot` and siblings, all in
  `Infomaterial/Language/Positing/Four.lean`; blueprint
  `chapters/recurring-four/08-four-by-universal-property.tex`). Any carrier
  with two bounded lattice orders, each monotone in the other, receives a
  unique bounds-preserving map from FOUR. The mechanism: interlacing squeezes
  the knowledge-join of the truth bounds against the knowledge top from both
  sides (four-line proof; the same argument gives all four exchange
  identities by swapping roles). The four bounds assemble a copy of FOUR
  whether you wanted one or not. FOUR is to interlaced bilattices what ‚Ñ§ is
  to rings. **All declarations zero-axiom.**

- **The record carrier has no top** (`Record.no_kTop`, `no_tTop`, `no_tBot`
  in `Infomaterial/Language/Positing/Record.lean`; blueprint
  `chapters/value-four-bilattice/06-the-record-sector.tex`). The honest
  evidence carrier ‚Äî tallies, ‚Ñï√ó‚Ñï, the twist product of the unbounded
  lattice (‚Ñï, min, max) with itself ‚Äî satisfies every interlaced law
  (`record_interlaced`) but three of the four bounds do not exist.
  **Zero-axiom.**

Together: ‚ä§ is not a fact about evidence. **‚ä§ is the point at infinity
minted by demanding the value space be bounded** ‚Äî the projective closure of
the evidence quadrant. Belnap's fourth value, treated for fifty years as a
logical primitive, is here a compactification artifact. When a future
depth-of-the-spine carrier "meets ‚ä§," ask first: where did its bound come
from? That question is now mathematically well-posed.

Hidden rhyme, worth developing: `Calculus/Probability/Dequantization.lean`
proves support is an exact semiring homomorphism from counting to Boolean
arithmetic (Maslov dequantization, discrete endpoints). The charge readout
`Record.charge` is that map applied once per polarity. **The Belnap charge
is the tropicalization of the evidence monoid.** Nobody has stated this in
the literature; the two modules prove it jointly without saying it.

## 2. Belnap logic is forced, not chosen

`Record.bottom_reflecting_hom_eq_charge`: any map from records to charges
preserving the four lattice operations, sending the empty record to ‚ä•‚Çñ and
only the empty record to ‚ä•‚Çñ, IS the positivity readout, pointwise. Proof
mechanism (useful pattern): truth-absorption at the empty record forces the
one-tick records (told-true-once must land on t because only t and ‚ä•
survive `x ‚àß‚Çú ‚ä• = ‚ä•`, and bottom-reflection kills ‚ä•; dually for f); then
knowledge-meets force all pure records; knowledge-join forces the mixed
ones. This is a **uniqueness-of-semantics theorem** ‚Äî rare anywhere. The
lossiness of the charge (`charge_not_injective`,
`charge_add_eq_charge_joinK` ‚Äî the shadow cannot distinguish the counting
merge from the idempotent join) is therefore not a defect of the readout
but a property of reading records four-valuedly *at all*.

## 3. The regime table measures deficiency, not dynamics

`Record.record_escapes_strict_finite` (zero-axiom): the tally increment is
knowledge-inflationary and monotone, yet no iterate is ever a settling
stage. `Charge.settles_by_three` ‚Äî a corpus headline ‚Äî is thereby demoted
from law to **cardinality artifact**: Œ∫ ‚â§ 3 was the chain height of a
four-element lattice, nothing more. Counterpoint in the same module:
`joinClosure_one_step` ‚Äî every join-bounded closure on records still
settles instantly. Exact dichotomy: it is the *carrier's unboundedness*,
not the dynamics, that opens the œâ-regime.

The re-founding is done: **the regime tower** (`Infomaterial.regime_tower`
in `Closure/Regime.lean`, zero-axiom capstone). The corpus regime column
(strict-finite / Scott / transfinite-bounded / aperiodic) is a **deficiency
column** ‚Äî each regime names what the carrier's order lacks ‚Äî and one
derived carrier family now inhabits all four rungs:

1. **FOUR** (bounded quotient): settles by stage three
   (`Charge.settles_by_three`) ‚Äî strict-finite, because bounded finite
   height.
2. **Record** (topless): the tally increment never settles at any finite
   stage (`record_escapes_strict_finite`) ‚Äî the œâ-regime, because no top.
3. **ORecord** (the completed record, œâ on each axis, in `Record.lean`): a
   bounded interlaced bilattice again (`oRecordInterlaced` ‚Äî so
   `four_initial` fires, `four_embeds`, ‚ä§ = the double infinity), on which
   the extended increment settles *exactly at stage œâ*
   (`settles_at_omega`: no finite arrival; the stage-œâ value is fixed and
   is the orbit's least upper bound) ‚Äî transfinite-bounded, because the
   bound is restored at infinity.
4. **The germ preorder** (record sequences under bounded-difference
   domination, `Record.DomBy`): not antisymmetric
   (`germ_order_not_antisymm` ‚Äî mutual domination without identity), and
   the tally bump is a lax closure on it (`tallyLaxClosure`) with genuine
   lax slack (`tally_lax_slack` ‚Äî the first inhabited `HasLaxSlack` in the
   tree; the KZ inequality holds at witness constant one, and its proof is
   reflexivity of the germ order, since the double bump literally is the
   single bump plus one) ‚Äî the aperiodic signature, because antisymmetry
   fails.

Useful diagnostic background (not a headline ‚Äî these were ordinary scoping
lemmas, and their only significance was telling us which carrier to build):
the tree had already noted, in several places, that its pre-tower carriers
lacked the needed structure ‚Äî `Closure/Ordinal.lean` ¬ßG (the ordinal
classifier's `aperiodic` is out of range), `LaxSlackDiagnosis` (slack needs
non-antisymmetry), the flasqueness of the FOUR-valued settling sheaf, and
the asserted regime data on the tiling side. Read those as the tower's
requirements specification, nothing more.

Also over the dyadic tower (`Closure/Odometer.lean`):
`tower_gluing_dichotomy` (zero-axiom) ‚Äî every FOUR-valued stage
accumulation is globally bounded, while a knowledge-monotone record-valued
accumulation exists with no global section. Bounded coefficients glue,
topless coefficients don't: the first derived fact underneath the
`cohomologyVanishes` table.

Extended, same day, to the full **œâ-escape profile**
(`Odometer.omega_escape_profile`, zero-axiom): the ‚Ñï-indexed escape exists
at the topless œâ-rung and *nowhere else* ‚Äî in particular the germ carrier,
though topless (`germ_no_top`), never escapes along ‚Ñï: every countable
family of germs is dominated by its diagonal running maximum
(`germ_omega_family_bounded`). So at the aperiodic rung the obstruction is
present but œâ-invisible ‚Äî the corpus's Œ∫ ‚â• œâ‚ÇÅ placement, derived. And the
lax slack is now a flux theorem (`topBump_flux`, zero-axiom): the
contradiction bump's orbit is a single point of the germ order (every
iterate germ-equivalent to the seed) while the data never repeats and the
‚ä§-mass exceeds the iterate count ‚Äî settling holds at the order level,
fails at the data level, on one dynamic. **Strange consequence**: the
derived escape invariant cuts the regime column at the œâ-rung only,
(T,F,T,T), whereas the stipulated `cohomologyVanishes` gate cuts it
(T,T,F,F) ‚Äî they disagree at BOTH middle rungs. The stipulated table is not
the accumulation-gluing invariant.

RESOLVED, same day (`Infomaterial.unattained_settling_gate`, zero-axiom):
the quantity the stipulated gate measures is **unattained settledness** ‚Äî
a settled value exists that no finite stage attains. FOUR: settled AND
attained (stage 3) ‚Üí gate true. Record: nothing settled (succPos fixes
nothing) ‚Üí gate true. ORecord: ‚ü®œâ,0‚ü© fixed, no finite stage equals it ‚Üí
gate false. Germ: the bump orbit is one point of the order while no stage
equals the next ‚Üí gate false. Matches `cohomologyVanishes` at all four
rungs. Reading (via `KappaStratification.landauer_cost_is_h1`: Landauer
bits = »û¬π, zero exactly on reversible nerves): the gate prices the
irreversible passage to a limit the stages never reach ‚Äî settledness
transcending attainment ‚Äî not coefficient boundedness. Every component was
already proved before the theorem was stated; the entire content was
noticing which four facts to conjoin. The trailhead was the corpus's
weave/tiling side (`AperiodicOrder/Tiling/WeaveDraft.lean` ‚Äî plain weave
as bilattice-coloured sofic shift, miscrossing = ‚ä§, entropy collapse ‚Äî
and `KappaStratification`'s Landauer/H¬π ledger), where the regime gate is
wired to irreversibility rather than to bounds.

## 4. Contradiction has an exchange-rate theory with three currencies

The endorsed ‚ä§/H¬π thread
(`Infomaterial/QuantumContextuality/CohomologicalContextuality.lean`,
blueprint `.../06-top-h1-exchange.tex`) plus this period's work gives
**three provably-or-plausibly distinct prices for one obstruction**:

1. **Per-contact price** = cycle rank (Euler count; linear-time). Theorem'd
   at PR (`pr_top_h1_exchange`: min ‚ä§-count = 1 = rank).
2. **Record mass** = what the faithful counting merge pays
   (`Record.topMass`; superadditivity `topMass_add` is the "second law":
   merging never destroys contradiction mass, where the idempotent join
   collapses it). THEOREM, same day
   (`QuantumContextuality.record_merge_ground_state`, general for all
   pair-context parity models): the minimum over realizing families of the
   counting merge's total mass equals the **ground-state energy** ‚Äî the
   minimum frustrated-context count over the gauge coset ‚Äî with NO
   vertex-cover correction. Proof shape worth remembering: lower bound via
   the majority readout (dissent from the majority = the smaller tally =
   the mass; each frustrated context contributes a dissenting incidence,
   and distinct contexts are distinct incidences even at a shared vertex);
   upper bound via the pay family (one tick per frustrated context at its
   picked endpoint, over a nodup measurement list). Instance comparisons
   also proved (`fig8_record_mass_attains_rank`,
   `theta_record_mass_below_rank`): figure-eight mass minimum = 2 = rank
   (the idempotent undercount disappears), theta-graph mass minimum = 1 <
   2 = rank (one shared frustrated edge services two topological debts) ‚Äî
   record mass and cycle rank are provably distinct invariants. Reusable
   trick: both lower bounds are one 3-Boolean lemma
   (`odd_triangle_frustrated`) applied once per odd cycle. The sheaf-level
   statement over the hull's cylinder covers is also proved ‚Äî see ¬ß5
   (`hull_settling_gluing_dichotomy`); `thm:record-settling-h1` is green.
   Tooling: watch for proof-term DEDUPLICATION in axiom audits ‚Äî a
   structure literal's `by decide` field can silently resolve to another
   definition's tainted `_proof_k` for the same statement (thetaNerve
   inherited prNerve's omega proof of `1 ‚â§ 4`); fix at the source.
3. **Idempotent-merge norm** = min over the coset of the min vertex-cover
   weight of the frustrated edges, degree-one measurements free (red node
   `thm:top-h1-exchange-rate`, deprioritized but proof-shape recorded and
   independently confirmed complete: lower bound reads a global assignment
   off the ‚ä§-free vertices ‚Äî any edge with both endpoints ‚ä§-free is
   unfrustrated, so the ‚ä§-set is a vertex cover; upper bound deviates each
   frustrated edge at a covering endpoint). NP-hard to evaluate in general.

Complexity asymmetry worth quoting: **the faithful invariants are cheap;
the lossy shadow is intractable.** Compression converts a linear-time
quantity into an NP-hard one.

External dictionary (reading, not theorem ‚Äî but `prConnection_flux` in
`DenseMatter/Quark.lean` already proves the first entry): this is ‚Ñ§/2
lattice gauge theory. Coset = gauge orbit; frustrated edges = Toulouse
frustration; minimizing over the coset = Ising spin-glass ground state;
merge ‚ä§-cells = toric-code syndromes/anyons; the figure-eight = two anyons
fused by an idempotent detector. Quantum error correction's quantitative
theory (code distance = min-weight coset representative; decoding =
syndrome inference) is a ready-made frontier map ‚Äî import its *questions*,
rederive finitely.

Also pending in this thread: the pair-context hypothesis excludes GHZ and
Mermin (three-element contexts) despite docstring gestures. The right
generalization is XOR constraint systems over hypergraphs = solvability of
a linear system over the two-element field; the all-versus-nothing
obstruction is target-not-in-row-space; Gaussian elimination, dependency-
free. Subsumes PR, GHZ, Mermin, magic square in one rank computation.

## 5. Collatz and the odometer share a tower

The parity coding conjugacy (`Closure/Collatz/ResidueGap.lean`: cylinders ‚âÖ
residues mod 2^k, coding 2-adic 1-Lipschitz) means **Collatz trajectories
are threads of the same 2-adic inverse tower whose limit is the Cantor
hull**. The system's hardest external conjecture (the parent-barrier gap ‚Äî
equivalently, a top-dyadic-slice avoidance statement for 3^a,
linear-forms-in-logarithms shaped) lives on the same carrier as the
odometer dynamics ‚Äî a useful co-location, whatever comes of it.

Mechanical state (operator-approved surgical move; do not reorganize
further): generic inverse limits live upstream at
`Closure/InverseLimit.lean` (`Infomaterial.InverseSystem`, `Thread`,
`Hull`, `hull_separated_by_stages`) and the dyadic Vershik odometer at
`Closure/Odometer.lean` (`Infomaterial.Odometer.vershik` + laws).
`AperiodicOrder/Tiling/InverseHull.lean` is now a pure instance module;
`CollatzTwoAdicLock`'s `twoAdicResidueSystem` resolves outward unchanged.
Built on top of that, same day: `dyadicTower` (prefix-restriction inverse
system), `dyadicHull_is_cantor` (threads ‚âÖ 2^‚Ñï, both round trips), and
`vershik_take` / `vershikStage_proj` / `vershikHull` ‚Äî the successor
commutes with prefix truncation, so the odometer descends to a dynamic on
the hull. DONE, same day: the record-coefficient settling sheaf over the hull's
cylinder covers (`Odometer.hull_settling_gluing_dichotomy`, zero-axiom):
`CylinderDatum` ‚Äî one value per cylinder, knowledge-monotone along
refinement, valued in a `PreValueCategory` ‚Äî glues for every charge-valued
datum and fails for the record-valued depth-tally datum, evaluated at a
hand-built all-false thread (`zeroThread`; `cantorThread`'s simp proofs
carry Quot.sound ‚Äî hand-build threads when cleanliness matters). This is
`thm:record-settling-h1` green: the coefficient carrier gates the settling
sheaf over an actual point-set cover, where the equality-agreement ƒåech H¬π
(`h1_vanishes`) sees nothing. The tower thread's last red is also resolved:
`thm:aperiodic-top-flux` is green via `unattained_settling_gate` (see ¬ß3) ‚Äî
the stipulated gate measures unattained settledness, and the tower
reproduces it exactly.

## 6. The endorsed program, in order (operator-ranked)

1. FOUR universal property ‚Äî DONE (zero-axiom).
2. Record sector ‚Äî DONE (flagship theorems zero-axiom; charge homs and
