   (`thm:record-settling-h1`), and `unattained_settling_gate`
   (`thm:aperiodic-top-flux` ‚Äî the stipulated gate derives as unattained
   settledness), all zero-axiom.
4. Hypergraph ùîΩ‚ÇÇ exchange (GHZ) ‚Äî see item 4 above.
5. Unify the five H¬π's ‚Äî the library has five distinct objects named H¬π
   (propositional ƒåech that always vanishes; CoverNerve Euler count;
   genuine quotient H¬π in `BigradedTruthKnowledgeLES` with its proved
   six-term LES and nonzero connecting map; ‚Ñ§/2 context-graph H¬π; causal
   order-complex H‚Åø). Only one pairwise exchange is proved. Identifying
   the CoverNerve count with the quotient H¬π rank for graph complexes is
   finite linear algebra, all in reach.

Selection criterion the operator set: prioritize frontiers that are
frontiers of THIS territory only ‚Äî not external math; failing that, proofs
that build the territory needed. "The rhetoric is 'obstruction generates
order' and doesn't matter ‚Äî the math does."

## 7. Pitfalls (each cost real time this period)

- **The `lean_run_code` MCP scratch server caches environments.** After a
  rebuild, `#print axioms` there can report STALE profiles (it showed
  Classical.choice on theorems that were clean). Decisive audit: write a
  scratch file and run `lake env lean` on it.
- **Core Nat min/max lemmas carry propext** (`Nat.max_le`, `Nat.le_min`,
  `Nat.min_eq_right`, even `Nat.succ_min_succ`). For zero-axiom work,
  hand-build from `Nat.le_max_left/right`, `Nat.min_le_left/right`,
  `Nat.not_succ_le_self`, `Nat.succ_ne_self`, `Nat.le_succ`,
  `Nat.succ_le_succ`, `Nat.zero_max`, `Nat.max_comm/assoc/self` ‚Äî those
  are clean. `omega` on max/min goals can pull Classical.choice.
- **omega does not see structure projections of literal constructors**
  (`{pos := ‚Ä¶}.pos` stays opaque): `simp only [defs]` first, or
  type-ascribe the component fact.
- **omega understands `max`/`min` notation but not `Nat.max` spelled
  directly.**
- **`rw` in abstract-carrier case bashes fails until `simp only [f]`
  reduces the match-def applied to constructors** (the boundsMap lesson);
  finish branches with an explicit `rfl` ‚Äî rw's auto-rfl is conservative.
- **Blueprint conventions**: definition boxes only in the primitive base ‚Äî
  structures elsewhere are `proposition` boxes with `thm:` labels; every
  node needs an upstream `\uses` edge or the rootless-node audit fires;
  moving Lean across namespaces requires updating blueprint `\lean{}`
  links AND Verso `{docstring ‚Ä¶}` references (grep both).
- **Namespace resolution saved the reorganization**: inside
  `Infomaterial.AperiodicOrder.Tiling`, an unqualified `InverseSystem`
  resolves outward to `Infomaterial.InverseSystem` ‚Äî instance modules
  survive an upstream extraction with zero edits.
- **Check your own conjectures against small strange cases before
  enshrining them** (the theta graph corrected the record-mass red node
  from "= cycle rank" to "= ground-state energy" before it shipped).
- **`simp` / `simp only` on match-definitions can pull `Classical.choice`**
  (it did in the œâ-settling proofs and in `domBy_trans`). The cure that
  worked every time: structural helper lemmas on the underlying type
  (the `oadd1` / `ole_refl` pattern), `nomatch` for impossible constructor
  equations, and hand-chained core lemmas (`Nat.le_trans` +
  `Nat.add_le_add_right` + `Nat.add_assoc ‚ñ∏ ‚Ä¶`) instead of omega. When a
  `‚ñ∏` cast fails on unreduced projections, `show` the defeq-reduced goal
  first.
- **getElem rewrites fail on proof-dependent motives**: use
  `List.getElem_of_eq` and `List.getElem_take` explicitly instead of `rw`.
- **A `def`'s proof fields count against every theorem that mentions it**:
  `#print axioms` traverses structure instances, so a choice-tainted
  lemma used inside a `PreValueCategory` field taints every downstream
  theorem. Audit instances, not just theorems.

