## 12b. The RH skeleton reading, ciphering, and cryptography (2026-07-11, same session, operator-endorsed)

Operator suspicion examined: "we are further along with RH than we've
realized." The defensible core, stated with the theorem/conjecture
discipline. The RH ecosystem decomposes into four load-bearing
components; the tree has proved pieces of three without reading them
as one thread.

1. **The Euler product is `fundamental_theorem_of_arithmetic`**
   (theorem, ¬ß12a). Œ∂(s) = ‚àè(1‚àíp‚ÅªÀ¢)‚Åª¬π *is* unique factorization read
   through an absolutely convergent sum; the tree owns the algebraic
   half, choice-free. Missing: only the Fourier/exponential layer
   already flagged at ¬ß10's unearned names and ¬ß9's Bishop
   investment.
2. **The trace-formula carrier is the odometer** (task open; closed
   forms in reach). Stage n is one cyclic rotation on 2‚Åø points
   (`vershikIter_reaches`), so Artin‚ÄìMazur periodic-point counts are
   all-or-nothing gated by 2‚Åø ‚à£ m; the zeta of a finite cyclic system
   is rational with zeros/poles at roots of unity ‚Äî on the unit
   circle, decidably. Weil proved the only RH ever proved (curves
   over finite fields) exactly as an Artin‚ÄìMazur count of Frobenius
   with eigenvalue-modulus conclusion ‚Äî the finite decidable idiom
   this tree speaks natively. That is the precise sense in which the
   suspicion is right: the tree builds the kind of zeta that has been
   tamed, not the kind that hasn't.
3. **The critical-line phenomenon is proved once, locally**
   (theorems): `zetaStar_phase_purePoint_iff_pisot` /
   `zetaStar_phase_singularContinuous_iff_salem` ‚Äî spectral purity ‚ü∫
   conjugate location against the unit circle, on a finite carrier.
   Salem is Lehmer's conjectural floor (the tree's flagged Bool-shadow
   debt), tying to Mahler measure and L-values (reading).
4. **The cycle-rank/Ihara identification** (conjecture, this session,
   believed unstated anywhere): the Ihara zeta determinant formula
   Œ∂_G(u)‚Åª¬π = (1‚àíu¬≤)^(r‚àí1)¬∑det(I ‚àí Au + Qu¬≤) carries the graph's
   cycle rank in the (1‚àíu¬≤) exponent ‚Äî the same invariant
   `pr_top_h1_exchange` proves is the per-contact ‚ä§-price. The Ihara
   zeta has its own RH, satisfied iff the graph is Ramanujan ‚Äî finite
   linear algebra per instance. A machine-checked "context graph's
   Ihara RH ‚ü∫ Ramanujan" (PR's 4-cycle as first instance) would weld
   the ‚ä§-ledger to a genuine zeta and is believed a first in any
   proof assistant.

**Ciphering (the coding/word side).** The parity-coding conjugacy
(cylinders ‚âÖ residues mod 2^k, 2-adic 1-Lipschitz, ¬ß5) is already a
proved *leakage theorem*: the first k parity symbols of a trajectory
reveal exactly the seed mod 2^k ‚Äî simultaneously an upper bound
(nothing beyond the residue) and an attack (the residue, fully).
`vershik` + `vershik_take` is structurally counter-mode keystream
generation whose truncation-compatibility theorem says the cipher
factors coherently through every precision level. Deeper (conjecture,
high-value): **strong contextuality is perfect secrecy** ‚Äî a one-time
pad is an empirical model with uniform local marginals and no
adversary-accessible global section; Abramsky-style no-global-section
(H¬π ‚â† 0) is what a secret-sharing scheme is. Re-read
`record_merge_ground_state` as the **price of forgery**: the minimum
‚ä§-mass an adversary must hold to force a globally consistent
transcript. Believed unstated in either literature; the Lean half is
green.

**Cryptography (the arithmetic side).** `ResidueGap.lean` already
contains the number-theoretic engine of RSA (B√©zout witnesses,
modular inverses from coprimality, cancellation, residue
characterizations) ‚Äî built for Collatz, reusable as-is. The missing
span is elementary: Fermat's little theorem and Euler's theorem over
the existing `ModEq`/`gcd` machinery, then **RSA correctness
(decrypt ‚àò encrypt = id) as a choice-free theorem** ‚Äî per ¬ß9, the
certified-numerics differentiator Mathlib cannot match (its
choice-saturated certificates are vacuous). Then the unconditional
**Monier‚ÄìRabin bound** (at most 1/4 of bases are strong liars ‚Äî
finite, witness-based) as Miller‚ÄìRabin soundness; the
GRH ‚áí deterministic-witness-bound theorem goes in as an honestly
conditional blueprint red node ‚Äî GRH's most concrete worldly
employment is as a warranty on prime certification, so the RH thread
and the crypto thread meet in one statement. Mascot instance
(decidable, near-free): **`carmichael_561`** ‚Äî 561 = 3¬∑11¬∑17 is the
least Carmichael number, a composite passing Fermat's test for every
coprime base: a convincing liar whose lie is locally unfalsifiable,
i.e. the exact object this library prices. The corpus's own name
becomes a theorem instead of a coincidence.

**Ranked telescope (operator-endorsed, extends ¬ß12a's program):**

1. Odometer Artin‚ÄìMazur zeta upgraded to the Weil-shaped statement:
   rationality + zeros/poles on the unit circle for the stage
   dynamics.
2. Ihara zeta of context graphs + the cycle-rank exponent
   identification; Ramanujan ‚ü∫ graph-RH instance on the PR 4-cycle.
3. The crypto spine: Fermat‚ÄìEuler ‚Üí RSA correctness ‚Üí Monier‚ÄìRabin ‚Üí
   `carmichael_561`.
4. Contextuality-as-secrecy: furthest from a theorem, largest prize;
