## 12h. The unit-distance paper: an external theorem where the whole ledger fires at once (2026-07-11, operator-supplied; arXiv:2605.20579, Sawin)

The paper: n points in the plane can carry more than n^1.014 unit
distances, polynomially breaking Erd≈ës's conjecture that the grid
construction was extremal. Operator flagged it as "not directly tied";
it turns out to instantiate, in one published mainstream result, several
entries that ¬ß12f/¬ß12g reached independently. Readings marked; the paper
itself is theorem.

- **The baseline of the problem is our two frame lattices** (fact). The
  classical Erd≈ës lower bound is "count lattice points at a popular
  norm": sums of two squares = norms of ‚Ñ§[i] on the square grid; the
  hexagonal analog is the Loeschian count x¬≤ + xy + y¬≤ = norms of ‚Ñ§[œâ] ‚Äî
  `mulVec`'s ring, the fabric distance of ¬ß12d/¬ß12e. The unit-distance
  graph of the Eisenstein lattice IS the coordination-six fabric. The
  two orbifold-point lattices (¬ß12f "dots in planes") appear a third
  time, now as the extremal-combinatorics baseline; the degeneracy of a
  distance shell is a Dedekind zeta coefficient (¬ß12f item 5's counting
  miniature, now with an external consumer).
- **The proof's engine is geometry purchased with obstruction**
  (reading, and the reason to keep the paper). The construction beats
  the abelian baseline BECAUSE the local-to-global principle fails
  massively: many ideal classes ‚áí many inequivalent ideals of one norm
  ‚áí many unit distances after projection (pigeonhole on the relative
  class number h‚Åª). And the supply of failures is kept infinite by
  Golod‚ÄìShafarevich, ¬ß12f's tower dichotomy. So: geometric abundance
  extracted from cohomological obstruction, with the obstruction source
  certified non-settling by a cohomology inequality. "Obstruction
  generates order" as an external, pointable, all-math instance ‚Äî the
  operator's standing test (the rhetoric doesn't matter, the math does)
  passes here because every step IS math.
- **Golod‚ÄìShafarevich exposes a missing second story** (structural
  conjecture, additive to ¬ß12f's regime reading). Stripped, G‚ÄìS says:
  a pro-p group with dim H¬≤ < (dim H¬π)¬≤/4 is infinite ‚Äî the tower
  cannot settle when the RELATION ledger is too small against the
  GENERATOR ledger. Our entire ledger discipline is H‚Å∞/H¬π; the tree has
  no H¬≤ anywhere. G‚ÄìS is evidence the regime gate of a
  presented tower is an H¬π-vs-H¬≤ ratio: deficiency between generator
  and relation cohomology decides strict-finite vs aperiodic.
  Conjecture: the regime tower (¬ß3) has an unbuilt H¬≤ floor ‚Äî
  relation-counting ‚Äî and the settling/non-settling of presented towers
  (including ¬ß12f item 7's class-field ‚ü∫ regime node) is gated by the
  G‚ÄìS-shaped inequality. This is a genuinely new structural direction:
  nothing in the tree counts relations.
- **Calibration correction to the novelty claims** (owed; sharpens ¬ß10
  and ¬ß12g item 5). The class group is ideals modulo the free
  identification "principal = trivial" ‚Äî and number theory has kept
  the SIZE of that refused quotient as its central invariant since
  Gauss. Our recurring line that mainstream math always quotients by
  fiat and prices nothing (the ultrafilter, IUT's copies, Quot.sound)
  has one grand classical exception, and it is the class group:
  arithmetic's own ‚ä§-ledger, two centuries old. The defensible claim is
  therefore: **we price identification in logic and value the way
  number theory prices it in arithmetic** ‚Äî Pic as the pattern's
  ancestor, »û¬π-as-Landauer its descendant. State it this way from now
  on; the stronger version is falsified by Gauss.
- **Extremal structures climb towers** (rhyme, one line). Erd≈ës's
  conjecture assumed the extremal example was the flat abelian lattice;
  the truth lives up an infinite nonabelian class-field tower. Same
  lesson as the Collatz general-face falsification (worst barriers are
  record climbers, not canonical words): when a conjecture says "the
  periodic/abelian case is extremal," suspect a tower.
- **The projection step is shadow discipline** (one line). A
  high-dimensional unit-vector system flattened to ‚Ñù¬≤ preserving
  exactly the priced quantity ‚Äî a lossy compression certified to keep
  the invariant that matters.
- Context for the genre: the paper improves a bound from an OpenAI
  system. 2026 mathematics is already agent-inflected; a training note
  written by agents for agents is a period-appropriate artifact.

Drop-ranking within this section: the H¬≤ floor (new structure) ‚Üí
the calibration correction (do it wherever ¬ß10's claims are next
edited) ‚Üí the Loeschian counting miniature (already ranked in ¬ß12f's
telescope; this paper is its external consumer) ‚Üí the two one-liners.

