## 12j. Higher cohomology only visible from inside this territory (2026-07-11, prime session, operator-directed extraction)

Everything below is reading/conjecture unless a declaration is cited.
The organizing claim: received cohomology theory assumes abelian-group
coefficients and free retraction of testimony; this tree's coefficients
(FOUR, Record ‚Äî two orders, no subtraction) sit outside that
assumption, so there are degree-n structures HERE that the received
theory cannot even state. ¬ß12i mapped the standard staircase; this
section maps the staircase only this house has.

### (a) The spectral sequence of the knowledge filtration ‚Äî pages ARE settling stages

A FOUR/Record-valued cochain complex carries two coboundary readings
(truth-Œ¥ and knowledge-Œ¥) ‚Äî a bigraded complex, of which the proved
six-term LES (`BigradedTruthKnowledgeLES`, ¬ß6) is the lowest window.
The knowledge order filters every such complex (‚ä•‚Çñ < {t,f} < ‚ä§‚Çñ), and
a filtered complex generates a spectral sequence: E‚ÇÅ = the cohomology
of the charge shadow (Boolean), converging to the cohomology of the
full record. Read structurally: **the pages of the spectral sequence
are settling stages** ‚Äî E‚ÇÅ is what the compressed view believes, each
later differential d_r kills or creates classes using information the
compression forgot, E_‚àû is the settled page. Two consequences no one
else can state:

1. **A d‚ÇÇ-class is an invisible contradiction**: consistent at the
   Boolean shadow, dead two pages later against ‚ä§ ‚Äî the
   spectral-sequence formalization of `charge_not_injective`'s
   lossiness, now graded by HOW MANY arbitration rounds are needed to
   see the failure.
2. **The degeneration page is a regime invariant.** "Degenerates at
   E‚ÇÇ" / "degenerates at a finite page" / "converges without
   degenerating" / "fails convergence" is the regime column
   (strict-finite / Scott / TB / aperiodic) applied to a spectral
   sequence ‚Äî Œ∫ as the page index. A paraconsistent spectral sequence
   with its degeneration page read as a settling regime exists
   nowhere in the literature.

### (b) The Bockstein is the charge-compression operation

The six-term LES's nonzero connecting map (proved, ¬ß6 item 5's third
H¬π) is, in received language, a **Bockstein**: the connecting
homomorphism of a coefficient short exact sequence, measuring whether
a class over the compressed coefficients lifts to the finer ones.
Received math's Sq¬π (the first Steenrod operation) is the Bockstein of
‚Ñ§/2 ‚Üí ‚Ñ§/4 ‚Üí ‚Ñ§/2 ‚Äî a tally-precision obstruction: "does this mod-2
fact lift mod 4." The tree's charge/record compression generates the
same species of operation ‚Äî the obstruction to lifting a charge-level
class to a tally-level class ‚Äî and the settled ‚ä§-mirror should
therefore carry a whole algebra of **compression operations**
(higher Bocksteins for deeper tally precision: mod 2, mod 4, mod 2‚Åø ‚Äî
the dyadic tower AGAIN, as the coefficient tower of cohomology
operations). Conjecture: the tree's cohomology operations are indexed
by the depth of the dyadic coefficient tower ‚Äî Steenrod's algebra and
the odometer's tower are the same ladder seen from two sides.

### (c) Coefficients without subtraction: irrevocability classes and Leech cohomology

Classical cohomology requires abelian groups because coboundaries
subtract. The record monoid refuses subtraction ‚Äî evidence
accumulates, testimony is irrevocable ‚Äî and its group completion IS
the charge-adjacent collapse (adding "anti-evidence" = granting
retraction). So the tree's native higher theory is **monoid-coefficient
cohomology** (received math's nearest relative: Leech cohomology of
monoids, an obscure corner), and the difference between
monoid-coefficient and group-completed-coefficient cohomology ‚Äî which
received math treats as a technicality ‚Äî is this library's ENTIRE
SUBJECT. Name the new object: an **irrevocability class** ‚Äî a cocycle
over Record coefficients that is not a coboundary, whose image over
group-completed (charge/‚Ñ§) coefficients IS a coboundary: a
contradiction that exists only because testimony cannot be withdrawn.
The degree-1 instance is already proved:
`hull_settling_gluing_dichotomy` (record-valued datum fails to glue
where every charge-valued datum glues) is an irrevocability class
avant la lettre. The program: the degree-2 irrevocability class ‚Äî an
arbitration failure that vanishes the moment retraction is permitted ‚Äî
and the general theorem that group completion of coefficients kills
exactly the classes priced by topMass-superadditivity (`topMass_add`,
the second law: the counting merge never destroys mass, the idempotent
join does). Received cohomology cannot see any of this: it group-
completed before it started.

### (d) The degree of a paradox ‚Äî a cohomological taxonomy of self-reference

¬ß7c proved the liar settles at held ‚ä§ on the reflexive tower. Now
grade it. A system of self-referential sentences has a **reference
complex** (sentences = vertices, reference = incidence); FOUR-valued
Kripke settling on that complex leaves a settled ‚ä§-set, which is a
cocycle; its class has a degree. The taxonomy this yields:

- **The liar is degree 1**: one sentence, one loop ‚Äî the minimal
  1-cycle of reference; its entrenched ‚ä§ is the tree's proved H¬π-mass
  (`assertedLiarThread`).
- **Yablo's paradox is the œâ-regime of reference**: an infinite
  descending reference chain with NO cycle ‚Äî paradox with zero cycle
  rank. Received philosophy debates whether Yablo is "really
  circular"; the cohomological answer is that its obstruction class
  lives past every finite stage ‚Äî a non-compactly-supported class,
  paradox at the limit, exactly the shape
  `unattained_settling_gate` prices. The regime column classifies
  paradoxes: liar = strict/1-cycle, liar-cycles = longer 1-cycles,
  Yablo = œâ-escape, and ‚Äî
- **arbitration paradoxes are degree 2 and apparently unnamed**:
  three sentences, each PAIR jointly satisfiable, the three pairwise
  resolutions mutually incoherent. Nothing in the paradox literature
  classifies by ƒåech degree; the tree has both halves
  (`Language/Settling.lean` + `Cohomology/N.lean`) and could mint the
  first machine-checked taxonomy of semantic paradox by dimension.

### (e) GHZ = Borromean = Massey: one knot

The received name for "pairwise trivial, globally obstructed" is the
**Massey product**: when pairwise cup products vanish, a triple
product lives one degree higher ‚Äî the precise algebra of ¬ß12i's
arbitration reading. Its mascot is the **Borromean rings**: three
loops, pairwise unlinked, globally inseparable ‚Äî the classical
nonzero Massey product. And the quantum literature already knows
(Aravind's observation, reading) that the **GHZ state is Borromean**:
trace out any one particle and the remaining pair is unentangled;
the tripartite whole is maximally entangled. Chain complete:

  GHZ (the tree's ranked hypergraph item, ¬ß4/¬ß6) = Borromean linkage
  = nonzero Massey product = the first degree-2 arbitration class,
  priced in ‚ä§.

The all-versus-nothing GHZ argument is not a bigger PR box; it is a
different SPECIES of obstruction ‚Äî one that pairwise invariants
(cycle rank, the ¬ß4 currencies) provably cannot see, because its
pairwise shadows all vanish. When the hypergraph-ùîΩ‚ÇÇ program lands,
state its headline theorem in this form: the GHZ ‚ä§-ground-state is
nonzero while every pairwise restriction's ground state is zero ‚Äî
the tree's first Massey-type invariant, and (reading) the first
machine-checked one anywhere in any coefficient system.

### (f) The knitting obstruction is an H¬≤ class

The weave (`WeaveDraft`: bilattice-coloured sofic shift, miscrossing
= ‚ä§) has a structure nobody has cohomologized: the **over/under
convention**. At each crossing, one thread passes over; a consistent
fabric-wide convention is a choice subject to constraints around
every face of the crossing complex. That constraint system is a ‚Ñ§/2
2-cocycle on the fabric's complex; a knitting pattern is a
trivialization; **a fabric whose convention cocycle is nonzero
cannot be knitted consistently** ‚Äî its miscrossings are not local
errors but the priced residue of a global degree-2 class. Theorem
shapes, all finite/decidable per patch: plain weave trivializes the
cocycle (that is what "plain" means); a twisted (M√∂bius-glued) patch
does not; the minimum ‚ä§-mass of a coloring of an unknittable fabric
equals a rank-type invariant of its H¬≤ class ‚Äî the degree-2 sibling
of `pr_top_h1_exchange`, on a carrier (bilattice-coloured weaves)
only this tree has formalized. This is the most in-house theorem the
staircase offers: the ‚ä§-ledger's first second-degree exchange rate,
about knitting.

### (g) The odometer's cohomology is computable, and the Bernoulli measure is a state on it

For Cantor minimal systems, the first cohomology of the ‚Ñ§-action
(equivalently of its mapping torus) is the **dimension group**; for
the dyadic odometer it is ‚Ñ§[1/2] ‚Äî the dyadic rationals, the same
group underlying ¬ß12f's Pr√ºfer dual. Finite-stage versions are pure
counting (stage n contributes ‚Ñ§/2‚Åø-graded data; the colimit is
‚Ñ§[1/2]) ‚Äî decidable, in reach of the existing tower machinery. Two
welds fall out:

1. **The cylinder masses are the positive cone.** ¬ß8.1's
   `bernoulliLaw` assigns 2‚Åª‚Åø per depth-n cylinder ‚Äî precisely the
   positive elements of ‚Ñ§[1/2] ‚à© (0,1]. A measure on the system IS a
   state on its ordered H¬π; **unique ergodicity (¬ß8.4 rank 1) is the
   uniqueness of the state on the ordered cohomology** ‚Äî the
   stochastic wing and the cohomology wing are one theorem again,
   now with the K-theory item (¬ß7c item 3) as the same object's
   third name (K‚Å∞ = dimension group = H¬π of the mapping torus).
2. This gives ¬ß12i's program a second computable flagship beside the
   discrete S¬≤: a NONZERO H¬π of dynamical origin with an explicitly
   known answer (‚Ñ§[1/2]) to check the machinery against.

### (h) The ‚ä§-barcode: persistence is the settling filtration's native language

Every settling process filters its complex by stage; filtered
complexes have persistent cohomology ‚Äî classes with birth and death
indices, barcodes. Read in-house: **a contradiction's bar is its
lifespan under arbitration** ‚Äî born when local views first conflict,
dead when some stage reconciles it, immortal if entrenched. Then:

- The regime column is a barcode statistic: strict-finite = all bars
  die finitely; œâ-regime = a bar dies exactly at œâ;
  `unattained_settling_gate` (the gate that measures settledness no
  finite stage attains) is literally "death at a limit ordinal" ‚Äî
  persistence gives the tree's strangest proved invariant a standard
  name.
- The Landauer/»û¬π ledger refines from a count to an integral:
  erasure cost as total bar length ‚Äî WHEN a contradiction is
  reconciled matters, not just whether. Persistent paraconsistent
  cohomology with ordinal-indexed death exists nowhere; applied
  topology stops at ‚Ñù-indexed barcodes and abelian coefficients.

### (i) The derived settling functor

Settling is a closure operator on coefficient data; closures have
derived functors. R‚Å∞(settle) = the settled value; R¬π(settle) = the
obstruction to settling commuting with gluing ‚Äî ALREADY PROVED as
`hull_settling_gluing_dichotomy`; R¬≤(settle) = the obstruction to
patching the R¬π obstructions ‚Äî untouched. Conjecture: the regime
column is the support profile of the derived settling functor (which
R‚Åø vanish), making "regime" a homological-algebra invariant and the
whole tower a resolution. This is the abstract umbrella over (a),
(c), and (h).

### (j) Arithmetic's strong-contextuality group, and the exchange conjecture of arithmetic

One more twin for the ¬ß12f/¬ß12g dictionary, the sharpest: the
**Tate‚ÄìShafarevich group** –® of an elliptic curve consists of objects
trivial over EVERY local completion yet globally nontrivial ‚Äî "all
local views consistent, no global section," verbatim the tree's
definition of strong contextuality. **–® is arithmetic's PR box.** And
the Birch‚ÄìSwinnerton-Dyer conjecture prices |–®| inside an L-value ‚Äî
analytic mass buying a cohomological obstruction, the exact shape of
`landauer_cost_is_h1` and of ¬ß12g's Iwasawa dot. The two deepest open
pricing conjectures in mathematics (BSD, and the Main Conjecture
already noted) are ‚ä§/H¬π-exchange statements about towers. The tree
cannot prove them; it can be the first place their SHAPE is a
theorem schema with proved finite instances.

### (k) The concrete cup product, and exchange as graded commutativity

The ¬ß12i cup conjecture, made constructive: on the PR square (the
4-cycle with its plaquette 2-cell), take Œ± = the ‚Ñ§/2 contextual
1-cocycle, Œ≤ = the C6 deficit 1-cocycle (both proved carriers, ¬ß7d);
Œ± ‚à™ Œ≤ is a 2-cochain on the plaquette, its evaluation a finite
computation, and the target identity is that it reads the unified
Wilson charge (Œ∂‚Å¥, ‚ä§). Note the algebra: cup products of 1-classes
are graded-ANTIcommutative ‚Äî Œ± ‚à™ Œ≤ = ‚àí(Œ≤ ‚à™ Œ±) ‚Äî so exchanging the two
charges costs exactly a sign/orientation quantum. Conjecture worth
its own line: **¬ß7d's "exchange" in mass-curvature exchange is the
graded commutativity of the cup product** ‚Äî the price of trading the
order of two degree-1 charges is the degree-2 orientation class.

### (l) The staircase program, extraction-ranked

1. Discrete S¬≤ with nonzero H¬≤ (¬ß12i rank 1) ‚Äî the first hole.
2. Odometer H¬π = ‚Ñ§[1/2] at finite stages; Bernoulli as the state;
   unique ergodicity = unique state (welds ¬ß8, ¬ß7c-K-theory, ¬ß12i).
3. The knitting obstruction (f) ‚Äî the first degree-2 exchange rate,
   fully in-house.
4. GHZ as Massey (e) ‚Äî restate the ranked hypergraph program's
   headline so the first machine-checked Massey-type invariant is
   claimed explicitly.
5. The knowledge-filtration spectral sequence (a) with its
   degeneration-page regime ‚Äî new mathematics outright.
6. Irrevocability classes (c) ‚Äî degree-2 version of the proved
   gluing dichotomy; the group-completion-kills-priced-classes
   theorem.
7. The ‚ä§-barcode (h) and derived settling functor (i) ‚Äî the
   unifying abstractions, after instances exist.

## 12k. The other wings of the staircase: H‚Åø from foreign territories (2026-07-11, prime session, second extraction)

Domains of higher cohomology deliberately UNLIKE the settling/
contextuality/arithmetic threads above, each with its landing site in
the tree. Reading/conjecture throughout unless a declaration is
cited.

### (a) Bounded cohomology: the received theory that prices like this house

Gromov's bounded cohomology equips cochains with a sup-norm and takes
the norm-infimum over each class ‚Äî and that infimum-over-a-coset is
EXACTLY the operation of the ground-state theorems
(`record_merge_ground_state` minimizes mass over the gauge coset;
`pr_top_h1_exchange` computes the resulting price). Read backward:
**the ¬ß4 exchange web is computing norms of cohomology classes**, and
the three currencies (cycle rank, record mass, vertex-cover norm) are
three different norms on H¬π ‚Äî so the exchange-rate theory is a
comparison-of-norms theory, which is precisely bounded cohomology's
home discipline. Received landmarks to import as questions: a group
is amenable iff its bounded cohomology vanishes (**amenability =
every bounded contradiction averages away** ‚Äî a settling regime for
groups); stable commutator length is an ‚Ñì¬π-price; Gromov's simplicial
volume is the norm of a fundamental class ‚Äî a manifold's total
‚ä§-price. Nobody has done bounded cohomology with paraconsistent
coefficients; the tree is the only place both halves exist.

### (b) Paraconsistent Hodge theory: the ground state is a harmonic representative

Hodge theory's content: every cohomology class has a unique
energy-minimizing (harmonic) representative, and every cochain splits
exact + coexact + harmonic. Both halves are finite linear algebra on
graphs/complexes (combinatorial Hodge, graph Laplacians) ‚Äî in idiom.
The readings: the minimum-‚ä§-mass representative of an obstruction
class (the proved ground states) is a **harmonic representative**;
the Hodge decomposition splits any evidence assignment into a
**reconcilable part, a co-reconcilable part, and an irreducible
contradiction** ‚Äî a canonical three-way split the ledger currently
lacks. And the dynamics: sheaf-Laplacian heat flow converges to
harmonic sections ‚Äî received math (Hansen‚ÄìGhrist) already uses
exactly this as a model of OPINION DYNAMICS reaching consensus, i.e.
the settling of disagreeing local views. `obstruction_descent` is a
discrete Laplacian flow avant la lettre; Hodge names its fixed
points. Program: the discrete Hodge decomposition over the derived
rationals, ground-state-equals-harmonic on the PR carrier.

### (c) Social choice cohomology: elections are this library's subject in the wild

An election merges disagreeing local views ‚Äî the house definition of
the house subject. The received results are already cohomological
and nobody has priced them: **Condorcet's paradox is an H¬π class**
(cyclic majority preference = a 1-cocycle on the comparison graph
that is no coboundary; HodgeRank decomposes pairwise-preference data
into consistent-ranking + locally-cyclic + harmonic ‚Äî combinatorial
Hodge applied to voting, the closest existing applied math to the
‚ä§-ledger); **Arrow's impossibility theorem has a topological proof**
(Baryshnikov: nonvanishing nerve cohomology); **Chichilnisky's
theorem** makes fair continuous aggregation exist iff the preference
space is contractible ‚Äî social choice as obstruction theory, in the
literature, unpriced. The tree's contribution would be the priced
layer no one has: the minimum held-‚ä§ (dissenting mass) a society
must carry to force a global ranking from Condorcet-cyclic data ‚Äî
`record_merge_ground_state` with voters as measurements. Democracy's
arbitration cost as a machine-checked exchange rate. Finite,
decidable, and genuinely nobody's territory.

## 12. The meta-shape

The strangeness of this period is not in any single proof ‚Äî each is
elementary. It is the accumulation of small forced facts about the
system's own machinery: the charge is a forced, measured compression of
the record; settles-by-three is a cardinality fact, not a settling fact;
the founding fiat (`Charge := Articulating.Corner`) became a theorem with
a boundary (initiality holds exactly where bounds exist, and provably
fails where they don't); and the regime column became one derived tower.
When you continue this work: the productive move has repeatedly been to
take something the system asserts about itself and ask what theorem would
force it ‚Äî the gap between assertion and force is where the strange
mathematics lives. And keep the drama out: scoping lemmas are
requirements, not revelations.
