### 8.3 Portfolio records and owed portfolio decisions

The existing Investment Review Board decision
`lib/emsenn/services/board-of-directors/services/executive-office/data/decision-records/fund-distributing-claude-borne-work-to-scripts-and-lesser-models.json`
opens only its stated bounded internal-capability pilot. It is the current
portfolio allocation relevant to the Hoare-script and lesser-model direction;
it does not fund the whole AME program or any candidate product system.

The existing portfolio/work trace for this concept includes
`lib/emsenn/services/board-of-directors/services/executive-office/data/tasks/charter-the-business-or-mission-analysis-instrument.json`,
`lib/emsenn/services/board-of-directors/services/executive-office/data/work-items/charter-the-organization-level-conops-writer.json`,
`lib/emsenn/services/board-of-directors/services/executive-office/data/tasks/name-the-mape-k-correspondence-in-the-conops.json`,
and
`lib/emsenn/data/work-items/2026/07/17/2026-07-17-work-items.jsonl`
record `state-the-firms-operating-concept-from-its-two-business-mission-analyses`.
They establish how the analysis and this concept reached the portfolio line;
they do not allocate a product line.

No existing Investment Review Board allocation, integrated-portfolio
checkpoint charter, or product-development charter presently binds the
Platform Node Inducer AME, the shared development/assurance service classes,
or the market, deception, and legitimacy candidate systems as product lines.
Those records are owed only after requirements analysis and a rulable
portfolio decision; this concept does not invent their future identifiers.

## 9. Open strategic decisions kept visible

The following choices remain outside this draft and are carried forward for
the committee or the appropriate sovereign enterprise:

- which first bounded customer demand constitutes the Platform Node Inducer
  AME's formation case and portfolio proposal;
- which recurring cross-enterprise capabilities deserve separate
  shared-service AMEs, rather than duties inside an existing enterprise;
- whether and when the market, deception, and legitimacy candidate classes
  become funded product lines after their stated evidence gates;
- whether root's distributed investment, checkpoint, and change-control
  separation answers any part of the rotating-chairmanship problem; the
  561-group rotating-chair question remains that sovereign settlement's own;
- who constitutes the strategy and development committee at its annual
  cadence;
- which exact formal statements connect enterprise formation, glassy
  settlement, informational lightcones, Hoare composition, and the relevant
  Obsmetrologia structures.

Until those decisions settle in their own records, this concept supplies
direction and boundaries without pretending that direction is an allocation
or that recognition is proof.
